ESPKit is an independent implementation of the Espressif serial bootloader
protocol. It contains no code from esptool, espefuse or espsecure
(GPL-2.0-or-later). Protocol constants, register addresses and timing values
are technical facts documented by Espressif. The ESP32 flash encryption key
tweak table (Sources/ESPSecure/FlashEncryption.swift) is a hardware fact
taken from the constants of espsecure; its use was established by
differential testing against espsecure, without reading its code.

Third-party components:

- esp-flasher-stub v2.0.0 (https://github.com/espressif/esp-flasher-stub)
  Copyright (c) 2025 Espressif Systems (Shanghai) CO LTD
  Flasher stub binaries, dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0. The release JSON
  files are embedded verbatim in Sources/ESPDevice/BundledStubs.swift,
  generated by Tools/generate-stubs.py.

- ESP-IDF eFuse tables (components/efuse/<chip>/esp_efuse_table.csv, v5.5.3)
  Copyright Espressif Systems (Shanghai) CO LTD, Apache-2.0. Input of
  Tools/efuse-codegen; Sources/ESPEfuse/Generated/ is derived from them.
  Register addresses come from ESP-IDF's soc/<chip>/register headers. Display
  labels (category, displayed name, field list, a few composite field
  descriptions) are aligned with the output of espefuse summary, used as a
  black box; no espefuse code or data file was used.
